module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.Affine
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.GlobalGeneration
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionOfSurfaces.RationalSingularities.BlowUpDualizingGeneration

/-!
# The global generation that clause (3) of Tag 0B64 consumes is its own conclusion

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] let `X` be the blowup of `Spec(A)` in the maximal ideal, let
`i : E ⟶ X` be its exceptional divisor and let `ω_X` be a dualizing module on `X`. Clause (3) of
[Stacks, Tag 0B64] is the surjectivity of the canonical map `f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X` of
[Stacks, Tag 0BBU], and `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_dualizingPullbackMap` of
`…/RationalSingularities/BlowUpDualizingGeneration.lean` proves it from the single datum

`G : ω_X|_E is generated by its global sections`,

the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0B5H].

This file proves the converse implication: the surjectivity of the canonical map gives `G`
back. The two are therefore equivalent: `G` is the conclusion of the clause restated on `E`, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.isZero_firstCohomology_curveTwist_iff_schemeTwist` of
`…/RationalSingularities/BlowUpDualizingCurveEquivalence.lean` shows for the curve vanishing
`hcurve` of clause (2).

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation`
  `.nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_epi`: if the canonical map of
  [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] is an epimorphism then the pullback of `ω_X` along *any* morphism into `X`
  is generated by its global sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_of_epi`:
  **the converse of clause (3)**, the same statement at the exceptional divisor, which is the
  input `G` of `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_dualizingPullbackMap`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_iff_epi`: the two
  are equivalent.

## The argument

The canonical map has source `f^*ω_A`, and *that* module is generated by its global sections for
a formal reason, with nothing assumed about `ω_A` beyond its being an `A`-module: the family of
all elements of `ω_A` spans `ω_A`, so `free ω_A ⟶ ω_A^~` is an epimorphism
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.tildeGeneratingSections`), and pullback along a morphism
of schemes carries global generating sections to global generating sections, being a left adjoint
which takes the structure sheaf to the structure sheaf
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.pullbackGeneratingSections`). Pulling back twice,
along `f` and then along an arbitrary `j : Z ⟶ X`, makes `j^*f^*ω_A` globally generated; pullback
preserves epimorphisms, again because it is a left adjoint; and the image of a generating family
under an epimorphism generates (`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.ofEpi`). So `j^*ω_X` is
globally generated.

No finiteness of `ω_A`, no coherence of `ω_X`, no property of `j` and no part of Situation
[Stacks, Tag 0B4W] beyond the existence of the canonical map enters; in particular the index type
of the resulting family is `ω_A` itself rather than a finite set.

## Normalizations

The normalization condition
`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.NormalizedDualizingModule` does not separate
`ω_X` from `ω_X(E)`: for `A = ℚ[x, y, z]/(xz - y²)` localized at the maximal ideal, the
conclusion of clause (3) fails at the normalized `𝒪_X(E)`, as the implementation notes of
`…/RationalSingularities/NormalizedDualizingModule.lean` record, and by the equivalence below so
does `G`. The stronger normalization `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation`
`.DualizingNormalization` of `…/RationalSingularities/NormalizedDualizingExistence.lean`, the
source's [Stacks, Remark 0B4R], pins `ω_X` down up to isomorphism; for it `G` is
[Stacks, Tag 0B5H] on `E`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B64](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B64)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BBU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BBU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4R)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace RationalSingularitySituation

variable (S : RationalSingularitySituation.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian S.X]

/-- **The pullback of `ω_A` along `f` is generated by its global sections**, with nothing
assumed about `ω_A`: all elements of `ω_A` span it, so `ω_A^~` is generated by global sections,
and pullback preserves that, being a left adjoint which takes the structure sheaf to the
structure sheaf. -/
public def generatingSectionsDualizingPullback (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) :
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback S.f).obj (tilde ωA)).GeneratingSections :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.pullbackGeneratingSections S.f _
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.tildeGeneratingSections
      (R := CommRingCat.of S.A) ωA (id : ωA → ωA)
      (by rw [Set.range_id, Submodule.span_univ]))

/-- **Surjectivity of the canonical map of [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] makes every pullback of `ω_X`
globally generated.** The source `f^*ω_A` of the canonical map is globally generated by
`generatingSectionsDualizingPullback`, pullback along `j` preserves both global generation and
epimorphisms, and the image of a generating family under an epimorphism generates.

At `j` the exceptional immersion this is the converse of clause (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64]; see
`AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_of_epi`. -/
public theorem nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_epi
    (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (ωX : S.X.Modules) (hωX : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingModule ωX)
    (D : S.DualizingTraceSequence ωA ωX)
    (h : Epi (S.dualizingPullbackMap ωA hωA ωX hωX D))
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (j : Z ⟶ S.X) :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback j).obj ωX).GeneratingSections := by
  let : (Scheme.Modules.pullback j).IsLeftAdjoint :=
    ⟨_, ⟨Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction j⟩⟩
  let := h
  have hpe : (Scheme.Modules.pullback j).PreservesEpimorphisms :=
    Functor.preservesEpimorphisms_of_isLeftAdjoint _
  let : Epi (C := SheafOfModules.{u} Z.ringCatSheaf)
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback j).map (S.dualizingPullbackMap ωA hωA ωX hωX D)) :=
    hpe.preserves (S.dualizingPullbackMap ωA hωA ωX hωX D)
  exact ⟨(Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.pullbackGeneratingSections j _
    (S.generatingSectionsDualizingPullback ωA)).ofEpi
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback j).map (S.dualizingPullbackMap ωA hωA ωX hωX D))⟩

end RationalSingularitySituation

namespace BlowUpDualizing

variable (S : RationalSingularitySituation.{u})

/-- **The converse of clause (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64]**: in Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] at the
blowup of `Spec(A)` in the maximal ideal, surjectivity of the canonical map `f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X` of
[Stacks, Tag 0BBU] gives back the global generation of `ω_X|_E` that
`AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_dualizingPullbackMap` consumes.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation`
`.nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_epi` at the exceptional
immersion. -/
public theorem nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_of_epi (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A)
    (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (ωX : (blowUpScheme S.A).Modules)
    (hωX : letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (blowUpScheme S.A) := isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingModule ωX)
    (D : (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).DualizingTraceSequence ωA ωX)
    (h : letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
        isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      Epi ((rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).dualizingPullbackMap ωA hωA ωX hωX D)) :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A)).obj ωX).GeneratingSections :=
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
    isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
  (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_epi
    ωA hωA ωX hωX D h (exceptionalImmersion S.A)

/-- **The global generation that clause (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64] consumes is equivalent to the
conclusion of that clause.** In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] with `A` not regular, at the blowup
of `Spec(A)` in the maximal ideal, for `ω_A` a dualizing module for `A`, `ω_X` a dualizing module
on `X` and `D` the datum of [Stacks, Tag 0BBU],

`(ω_X|_E is generated by its global sections) ↔ (f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X is surjective)`.

The forward implication is `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_dualizingPullbackMap` and the
backward one is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_of_epi`. -/
public theorem nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_iff_epi
    (hnot : ¬ IsRegularLocalRing S.A) (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A)
    (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (ωX : (blowUpScheme S.A).Modules)
    (hωX : letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (blowUpScheme S.A) := isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingModule ωX)
    (D : (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).DualizingTraceSequence ωA ωX) :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A)).obj ωX).GeneratingSections ↔
      letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
        isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      Epi ((rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).dualizingPullbackMap ωA hωA ωX hωX D) :=
  ⟨fun ⟨G⟩ => epi_dualizingPullbackMap S hnot ωA hωA ωX hωX G D,
    nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_of_epi S ωA hωA ωX hωX D⟩

end BlowUpDualizing

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
